sequenceDiagram
  participant GH as GitHub event source
  participant APP as GitHub App installation
  participant CP as Agentic Delivery Control Plane
  participant ENROLL as Control Plane participant contract
  participant ORIGIN as Origin repository
  participant TYPES as Native Issue Type on issue
  participant DEFINITIONS as Organization issue-field definitions API
  participant VALUES as Per-issue field values API

  GH->>APP: subscribed issue or review event
  APP->>APP: apply installation access and deliver event
  APP->>CP: event envelope with repository ID
  CP->>ENROLL: check selected repository and exact participant pins
  Note over APP,ENROLL: App installation access and Control Plane enrollment are separate checks
  CP->>ORIGIN: re-fetch issue, repository identity, and native Issue Type
  CP->>DEFINITIONS: read organization field definitions and option IDs
  CP->>VALUES: read this issue's field values using repository permissions
  Note over TYPES,ORIGIN: Organization Issue Type definitions and an issue's native type value are related but distinct surfaces
  Note over TYPES,VALUES: Issue Type, lifecycle position, delivery authorization, governance metadata, and runner state remain distinct
  CP->>CP: interpret intent; propose route and field values
  CP->>CP: deterministically validate identity, permission, schema, option, transition, and orchestration contracts
  CP->>ORIGIN: mutate only the originating issue or branch after gates pass
  CP->>VALUES: write only validated per-issue field values
  Note over CP,VALUES: GitHub Projects fields are a separate surface and are not this lifecycle contract; issue-value writes do not change org field definitions
  CP-->>GH: publish evidence and origin write-back links
  Note over GH,ORIGIN: Target sequence; the 2026-09-24 live audit had no passing end-to-end run
